   Circuits and Systems (DDECS), Prague, CZECH REPUBLIC, APR 06-08, 2022},
Abstract = {The paper explores hardware supports for replaying instructions to
   protect processors against some fault injection attacks. A replay
   instruction is added to the instruction set of a small 32-bit RISC
   processor to allow the automatic and parametrized replay of sequences of
   instructions. Various detection elements are added to the processor,
   implemented on FPGA, and compared in terms of performances, cost and
   fault coverage. The proposed extension leads to significant improvements
   compared to software protections for a small silicon overhead.},
