Note = {22nd International Conference on Embedded Computer Systems -
   Architectures, Modeling, and Simulation (SAMOS), Samos, GREECE, JUL
   03-07, 2022},
Abstract = {Thermal control is a key aspect of large-scale HPC centers, where a
   large number of computing elements is employed. Temperature is directly
   related to both reliability, as excessing heating of components leads to
   a shorter lifespan and increased fault probability, and power
   efficiency, since a large fragment of power is used in the cooling
   system itself. In this paper, we introduce the TEXTAROSSA approach to
   thermal control, which couples innovative two-phase cooling with
   multi-level thermal control strategies able to address thermal issues at
   system and node level.},
