   Ideas and Emerging Results (ICSE-NIER), Pittsburgh, PA, MAY 22-27, 2022},
Abstract = {Coverage-guided fuzzing is a popular tool for finding bugs. This paper
   introduces mu(2), a strategy for extending coverage-guided fuzzing with
   mutation analysis, which previous work has found to be better correlated
   with test effectiveness than code coverage. mu(2) was implemented in
   Java using the JQF framework and the default mutations used by PIT.
   Initial evaluation shows increased performance when using mu(2) as
   compared to coverage-guided fuzzing.},
