Abstract = {It is vital to select microarchitectures to achieve good trade-offs
   between performance, power, and area in the chip development cycle.
   Combining high-level hardware description languages and optimization of
   electronic design automation tools empowers microarchitecture
   exploration at the circuit level. Due to the extremely large design
   space and high runtime cost to evaluate a microarchitecture, ICCAD 2022
   CAD Contest Problem C calls for an effective design space exploration
   algorithm to solve the problem. We formulate the research topic as a
   contest problem and provide benchmark suites, contest benchmark
   platforms, etc., for all contestants to innovate and estimate their
   algorithms.},
