Year = {2022},
Pages = {86-91},
Note = {35th International Conference on VLSI Design (VLSID) / 21st
   International Conference on Embedded Systems (ES), ELECTR NETWORK, FEB
   26-MAR 02, 2022},
Abstract = {With the increasing number of processing elements or IP cores in a
   System-on-Chip, Network-on-Chip has become a better solution for on-chip
   interconnection. RISC-V is an open ISA specification that is strongly
   growing in the industry as well as academia. In this paper, we have
   designed and implemented a Network Interface (NI) architecture that can
   adapt a 32-bit RISC-V core to the on-chip communication framework. The
   functionality of the design is verified with the behavioral simulations
   done using Xilinx Vivado software tool. The design is implemented on an
   FPGA using ZedBoard. The performance parameters of the designed NI
   architecture are evaluated using Cadence RTL compiler and are found to
   consume considerably lesser area and power compared with the existing NI
   architectures in the literature. The behavioural simulations show that
   the proposed design shows improvement in latency as well compared with
   the prior work in literature.},
